# Azure PowerShell Identity Lab — Chewbacca and the GCP_Admins Group

## Objective

In this lab, you will use PowerShell to manage identities and permissions in Microsoft Entra ID.

You will:

1. Create a user named **Chewbacca**.
2. Create a security group named **GCP_Admins**.
3. Assign the **Global Administrator** role to the `GCP_Admins` group.
4. Add **Chewbacca** to the `GCP_Admins` group.
5. Verify each change using PowerShell.

> **LAB ENVIRONMENT ONLY**
>
> `Global Administrator` is one of the most powerful roles in Microsoft Entra ID. Use this exercise only in the classroom/test tenant provided for this lab.
>
> Production environments should follow least-privilege principles rather than routinely assigning Global Administrator access.

---

# Architecture

The end result of this lab will look like this:

```text
Microsoft Entra ID
       |
       +---- User
       |       |
       |       +---- Chewbacca
       |
       +---- Security Group
               |
               +---- GCP_Admins
                      |
                      +---- Global Administrator Role
                      |
                      +---- Member: Chewbacca
```

The important concept is:

```text
Chewbacca
    |
    v
Member of GCP_Admins
    |
    v
GCP_Admins has Global Administrator
    |
    v
Chewbacca receives the group's administrative privileges
```

