# Gate 3 — Define Your Lab Environment

Before creating Chewbacca, identify your Microsoft Entra tenant domain.

Your environment will probably have a domain similar to:

```text
something.onmicrosoft.com
```

Set your tenant domain:

```powershell
$TenantDomain = "YOURTENANT.onmicrosoft.com"
```

Create Chewbacca's User Principal Name:

```powershell
$ChewbaccaUPN = "chewbacca@$TenantDomain"
```

Display the result:

```powershell
$ChewbaccaUPN
```

It should look similar to:

```text
chewbacca@YOURTENANT.onmicrosoft.com
```

---

# Gate 4 — Create Chewbacca

First, specify a temporary lab password.

Replace the example below with a password appropriate for your lab environment:

```powershell
$InitialPassword = "<YOUR-TEMPORARY-LAB-PASSWORD>"
```

Now define the properties of the new user:

```powershell
$UserParams = @{
    accountEnabled = $true
    displayName = "Chewbacca"
    mailNickname = "chewbacca"
    userPrincipalName = $ChewbaccaUPN

    passwordProfile = @{
        forceChangePasswordNextSignIn = $true
        password = $InitialPassword
    }
}
```

Create the user:

```powershell
$Chewbacca = New-MgUser -BodyParameter $UserParams
```

Notice that the result of the command was saved in a variable:

```powershell
$Chewbacca
```

Now inspect some of the properties of the object:

```powershell
$Chewbacca.DisplayName

$Chewbacca.UserPrincipalName

$Chewbacca.Id
```

---

## Verify Chewbacca

Retrieve Chewbacca directly from Microsoft Entra ID:

```powershell
Get-MgUser -UserId $Chewbacca.Id
```

For cleaner output:

```powershell
Get-MgUser -UserId $Chewbacca.Id |
    Select-Object DisplayName, UserPrincipalName, Id
```

Expected result:

```text
DisplayName   UserPrincipalName                     Id
-----------   -----------------                     --
Chewbacca     chewbacca@YOURTENANT.onmicrosoft.com  <GUID>
```

### Important PowerShell Concept

The command did not simply return text.

It returned an **object**.

Try:

```powershell
$Chewbacca | Get-Member
```

Look through the properties and methods available on the object.

